scn 1
# battle-field (250 a side): two roster-quartile armies (sight 256/320/400, turn
# 1000/2500, footprint 2/3, speed 1.6..2.6, gun 160 px / 25 / 1 s) attack-move
# (fight) onto each other's start across open ground. The windows
# (`legion_cost window` lines below; tools/legion_cost.py battle) are start (the
# first field builds), march (before the armies see each other), contact (they
# meet and die) and mop-up (the survivors). A window's Legion work is the
# difference of two runs to its ends (--ticks). Wall time is reported by the
# runner, never gated.
# legion_cost window start 0 200
# legion_cost window march 200 500
# legion_cost window contact 500 2800
# legion_cost window mopup 2800 3600
name battle-field-2x250
ticks 3600
seed 7
players 2
weapons on
map flat 320 180
type r roster
group A 0 r 250 rect 6 6 70 174 pitch=5
group B 1 r 250 rect 250 6 314 174 pitch=5
at 1 fight A @B
at 1 fight B @A
